# --- R session / IDE artifacts ---
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Renviron

# --- Compiled Stan models and saved R objects ---
# rstan (auto_write = TRUE) writes a compiled *.rds next to each *.stan on first
# build; saved model fits and other intermediate R objects also use *.rds / *.rda.
# These are machine-local build artifacts and are regenerable, so they are not
# version-controlled.
*.rds
*.RDS
*.rda
*.Rda
*.RDa

# --- Local data caches ---
# Nothing in the pipeline fetches over the network any more: the weather-tide
# module, which cached NOAA CO-OPS / NDBC / ASOS / GSOD series under
# cache/weather_tide/, was removed 2026-09-13 (CHANGE_REGISTER A29). These rules
# are kept as a generic guard so a machine-local cache can never be committed.
cache/
*_cache/
*.cache

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
.RDataTmp

# --- R Markdown intermediate render artifacts ---
# rmarkdown writes figures/deps to <report>_files/ next to the .Rmd during a
# render and normally deletes it once the self-contained HTML is built; an
# interrupted render (e.g. a killed or hung fit) leaves it behind. It is a
# regenerable build artifact, so it is never tracked.
*_files/
# ...but 04_input_files/ is a real, version-controlled input directory whose name
# happens to end in "_files", so the glob above would silently untrack every NEW
# file dropped into it (the existing inputs are tracked only because they predate
# the rule). Re-include it explicitly so next season's data files are not lost.
!04_input_files/
!04_input_files/**

# --- Saved R workspaces ---
# RMD runs may dump a *_workspace.RData into their output/<date>/<model>/ folder.
# These are large, regenerable, and machine-local, so they are not tracked. This
# general glob replaces an earlier rule that ignored a single dated workspace path
# (output/20260619/...), which no longer matched after the 05_output/ rename.
*.RData
# (.Rproj.user/ above already covers everything RStudio writes; two duplicate
# .Rproj.user/shared/notebooks/paths lines were removed 2026-09-13. The five files
# that were TRACKED despite line 2 were untracked the same day: .gitignore never
# affects a path git is already tracking, so `git rm --cached` is the only fix, and
# harness section 71 now asserts that no ignored path is tracked again. One of the
# five, shared/notebooks/paths, is a table of LOCAL ABSOLUTE PATHS from a
# contributor's machine, which is a leak rather than clutter.)

# Rendered driver reports belong in the run folder under 05_output/, never beside the
# .Rmd. rmarkdown::render() writes there by default and a batch runner must move it; on
# 2026-09-04 two stages rendered in sequence and the second overwrote the first (see
# 07_documentation/development_notes/PIPELINE_STATUS.md section 1j).
01_BSS_models/*.html

# Patch files are a transport format, not repository content. Five have been committed
# by accident since 2026-08-25; each is a duplicate of a commit already in the history.
*.patch
